*.bak
*.swp

# ── This house's own block, since 2026-09-14 ──────────────────────────────
# ⚠️ In .gitignore, `#` only opens a comment at the start of a line. A comment
# at the end would be part of the pattern, and the rule would then match
# nothing, in silence. That is why every explanation gets its own line.

# How this house works: it cites the workshop trunk and means nothing outside
# it.
CLAUDE.md
# The agent's local permissions and settings. They have carried a credential.
# «This is not published». It has carried the zero since 2026-09-12, and rules
# that said `OFFLINE` without it had matched nothing ever since.
0OFFLINE/
# PIDs and logs of the house servers.
.servers/
# Telethon sessions: a whole key, they get in with no password.
*.session

# ── Secretos y entorno ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env.*
programming-keys.yaml

# ── Common block of the house, completed 2026-09-15 ───────────────────────
# Whatever a service here writes while it runs. Machine paths and, when
# something fails, whole tracebacks: the record of a run, not of the program.
# It goes in even where nothing writes a log yet, because the day something
# starts to, nobody will remember to come back and add the rule.
logs/
